109
00:04:29.650 --> 00:04:30.110
All right.

110
00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:31.390
Fast fact number two.

111
00:04:31.630 --> 00:04:33.490
This film was shot in Alberta, Canada.

112
00:04:33.890 --> 00:04:40.730
It was shot between August and November 1996 in Banff National Park, Canmore, Edmonton,

113
00:04:41.250 --> 00:04:43.970
Thunderstone Quarries, and Fortress Mountain Resort.

114
00:04:43.970 --> 00:04:49.150
And here is an audio clip of director Lee Tamahori talking about the location.

115
00:04:50.090 --> 00:04:54.870
We really needed to take this film somewhere that people haven't really been before, so

116
00:04:54.870 --> 00:04:56.270
it needed to look very, very rugged.

117
00:04:56.450 --> 00:04:57.990
You can't really fake that.

118
00:04:58.070 --> 00:05:01.470
You've got to take the actors and everybody into this environment.

119
00:05:01.630 --> 00:05:03.670
Give me your best fair confrontation.

120
00:05:03.890 --> 00:05:08.470
They lost right in the heart of the wilderness, and you've got to know how to survive.

121
00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:13.790
What I like about all of David Mamet's work is that it's extremely primal.

122
00:05:13.890 --> 00:05:18.110
It's one guy pitted against another guy, two guys pitted against the wilderness.

123
00:05:18.570 --> 00:05:22.910
When you take actors, the likes of Tony, who's never been exposed to this type of harrowing

124
00:05:22.910 --> 00:05:25.230
location, it braces them up more.

125
00:05:25.810 --> 00:05:28.030
So, lady, they were really out there.

126
00:05:28.270 --> 00:05:31.230
The actors, the crew, in the wilderness.

127
00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:34.030
I want to paint a little picture for you.

128
00:05:34.870 --> 00:05:42.270
The temperatures in Banff National Park in August are a high of 62 and a low of 33.

129
00:05:42.750 --> 00:05:49.070
But when we get to November, the high is 24 degrees and the low is 3.

130
00:05:49.510 --> 00:05:51.250
Yeah, that's not a lot.

131
00:05:51.790 --> 00:05:55.930
Josh went on a hiking trip with his college buddies there and absolutely loved it.

132
00:05:56.050 --> 00:05:57.530
But it is rugged terrain.

133
00:05:57.530 --> 00:05:58.110
Yes.

134
00:05:58.430 --> 00:06:01.230
These fellas spend a lot of time in water.

135
00:06:01.470 --> 00:06:03.010
I check the seawater temperatures.

136
00:06:03.010 --> 00:06:06.810
In August, they're around 54 to 61 degrees.

137
00:06:07.510 --> 00:06:11.290
For reference, I keep my cold dip tank around 60 degrees.

138
00:06:11.470 --> 00:06:15.250
I sit in it for one minute, and I go pretty numb in about 30 seconds.

139
00:06:15.690 --> 00:06:19.510
In November, the water gets as low as like 50 degrees.

140
00:06:19.790 --> 00:06:21.410
And they really got in it.

141
00:06:21.590 --> 00:06:21.810
Yeah.

142
00:06:21.970 --> 00:06:24.510
Like that wasn't like a soundstage or something.

143
00:06:24.710 --> 00:06:25.850
No, they look cold.

144
00:06:25.850 --> 00:06:27.490
And they don't warm the water.

145
00:06:27.610 --> 00:06:29.290
Obviously, it's seawater.

146
00:06:29.470 --> 00:06:29.970
It's water.

147
00:06:30.150 --> 00:06:31.090
It's natural water.

148
00:06:31.230 --> 00:06:33.230
You can't warm a park, a lake.

149
00:06:33.470 --> 00:06:33.890
Correct.

150
00:06:34.230 --> 00:06:34.490
Yeah.

151
00:06:34.910 --> 00:06:35.770
They're in it.

152
00:06:35.950 --> 00:06:36.610
They're in it.

153
00:06:37.070 --> 00:06:37.470
All right.

154
00:06:37.850 --> 00:06:39.630
Well, I've told you the characters.

155
00:06:39.630 --> 00:06:41.110
I've told you the location.

